originality.positioning_vs_prior_work.reason:
The Introduction relates CETV to the closest published families:
- variance and information criteria, and SMART/gSMART;
- CV-error global-accuracy criteria such as SFCVT, MEPE and TEAD. It argues they transport a scalar residual that assumes one failure mechanism, or over-exploit detected features;
- space-filling designs, which ignore remaining difficulty.

It then states CETV's distinct contribution: an observation-gated structural teacher whose disagreement with an unchanged reporter is calibrated on LOO residuals and weighted by unresolved volume. Weakness: committee-disagreement (QBC-style) and Voronoi-volume hybrid designs are not explicitly discussed, although 'model disagreement' is named.

writing_quality.limitations_discussed.reason:
